ble, it is assumed that women who did not give birth in health facility did not receive a c-section. Stillbirths are fetal deaths in pregnancies lasting 28 or more weeks. When pregnancy duration is reported in months, stillbirths are fetal deaths in pregnancies lasting 7 or more months. An asterisk indicates a figure is based on fewer than 25 unweighted cases and has been suppressed."},{"table":"9.8","note":"1 Birth order refers to the order of the birth among the respondent's live births."},{"table":"9.8","note":"2 Includes only the most recent birth in the 2 years preceding the survey."},{"table":"9.8","note":"3"},{"table":"9.8","note":"No education includes informal education (madrassa/duksi/adult education) and more than secondary includes middle-level colleges and universities. Secondary includes individuals who reported vocational training as the highest education level attended. Where a respondent's highest level attended is junior school, they are considered as having attained secondary level but not having completed it"}]}
